# Project Understanding Documentation

After a client call, when asked to convert its transcript into project understanding documentation for later human or AI planning, follow `AGENTS.md` and `.agents/skills/project-understanding/SKILL.md`.

This workflow is strictly read-and-document:

- Read repository files and supplied transcript content.
- For the default from-scratch mode, use only the transcript as product evidence; inspect current code only when explicitly requested for codebase alignment.
- Require the client-call transcript; ask for it if it is missing.
- Ask focused questions instead of silently assuming missing or ambiguous requirements.
- Run an iterative transcript grill inside the delegated subagent: write numbered, evidence-backed questions to `docs/project/open-questions.md`, present them, and stop until answered.
- The delegated subagent must automatically install the official `grill-with-docs`, `grilling`, and `domain-modeling` skills with `npx` when they are missing.
- Distinguish verified facts, explicit transcript requirements, inferences, and unknowns.
- Write only Markdown files under `docs/project/`.
- Never modify code, configuration, dependencies, generated files, tests, scripts, agent rules, or project structure.
- Never run project generators, formatters, analyzers, builds, dependency installs, migrations, or setup commands. The delegated subagent may install only the official agent-skill dependencies when they are missing.
- If required answers are unavailable, write only `docs/project/open-questions.md` and stop.
- Generate a useful provisional transcript-only package marked `Draft — questions pending` even while blocking questions remain; after answers, finalize it automatically without another confirmation.
